## Human intervention needed

The automated job failed during `setup/normal_setup()` while generating metadata for `org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.4`; it never reached native-image repair or metrics collection.

Preserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9929-fails-native-image-run-org.springframework-spring-context-6.0.4-7b26602f

All three `fixTestNativeImageRun` attempts failed in `generatePredefinedCglibProxyClasses`. The Native Image agent instrumented that helper task, causing Spring to treat the JVM as image code and throw `UnsupportedOperationException: CGLIB runtime enhancement not supported on native image`. No `6.0.4` test project, metadata, dynamic-access coverage, or publication metrics were produced; the continuation marker records `setupDone: false` and `publicationMetrics: null`.

Inspect:
- `logs/org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.4/native-image-run-fix/fixTestNativeImageRun-2026-10-07T16-31-56-416681Z.log`
- `logs/org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.4/native-image-run-fix/fixTestNativeImageRun-2026-10-07T00-54-25-830997Z.log`
- `logs/org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.4/library-preparation-preflight/claude-code.log`

Manual next steps:
1. Configure `generatePredefinedCglibProxyClasses` to run without Native Image agent instrumentation during metadata generation.
2. Rerun `fixTestNativeImageRun` for `6.0.4`, then run the full native test to expose and diagnose the original runtime failure.
3. After the tests pass, regenerate and validate metadata, dynamic-access coverage, and execution metrics.
